.TH ABOUT 1.SH NAMEabout \- what this collection knows about a program.SH SYNOPSIS\fBabout\fRprogram ....SH DESCRIPTION\fBabout\fRgathers, for each program named, everything the disk records about itin one place: its entry in\fBDOC/INDEX\fR(what it is), its category from\fBDOC/CATEGORIES\fR(what it is for), its line in\fBDOC/ORIGINS\fR(where it came from), the files it opens from\fBDOC/DEPENDS\fRwith whether each is here, whether its source is under\fBSRC\fR,\fRwhether it has documentation under\fBDOC\fR,\fRand the command to try..nf    about hack.fiIt finds the collection by looking for\fBDOC/INDEX\fRon the devices it could be mounted as, so it works with the disk as\fB/dd\fRor beside your own system.  A name the index does not have is answered\fBnot in DOC/INDEX\fR.\fR.PPWritten for this collection; the source is\fBSRC/keep/about.c\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOkeep, man